# Android Emulator Build System (`android/build/`)

The Android Emulator uses a **CMake + Ninja** build system driven by a Python
task runner.

## Directory Overview

- **`python/aemu/`**:

  - The Python build orchestrator invoked by `android/rebuild.sh` (Linux/macOS)
    and `android\rebuild.cmd` (Windows).
  - **`cmake.py`**: Main CLI entry point defining build flags (`--target`,
    `--config`, `--task`, `--sanitizer`, `--crash`, `--ccache`, `--feature`,
    `--prebuilts`) and sequencing build tasks.
  - **`tasks/`**: Individual pipeline tasks:
    - `prebuilts.py`: Builds or verifies third-party prebuilts when requested.
    - `configure.py`: Invokes prebuilt `cmake` with the appropriate toolchain
      file (`android/build/cmake/toolchain-<target>.cmake`), `sccache`, and
      feature flags to generate `objs/build.ninja`.
    - `compile.py`: Runs `cmake --build objs --target install` to compile all
      targets, assemble `objs/distribution/emulator/`, and strip/extract debug
      symbols.
    - `unit_tests.py`: Runs `ctest` (`CTestTask`) with the required
      SwiftShader/ANGLE/Vulkan runtime environment variables.
    - `distribution.py` / `package_samples.py`: Packages SDK release zip
      archives (`sdk-repo-<host>-emulator-<build_id>.zip`).
    - `emugen_test.py` / `integration_tests.py`: Additional test tasks.
  - **`platform/` & `process/`**: Host toolchain discovery, Visual Studio
    environment discovery (`vswhere.exe` / `vcvars64.bat` on Windows), and
    subprocess execution helpers.
  - **`prebuilts/`**: Recipes for building third-party prebuilts (`qt.py`,
    `angle.py`, `moltenvk.py`, `vulkan_loader.py`, `sdl2.py`).

- **`cmake/`**:

  - CMake toolchain files and helper modules used across the emulator build:
    - `toolchain.cmake` and `toolchain-<os>-<arch>.cmake`: Cross-platform
      compiler, linker, sysroot, and SDK configuration for Linux (`x86_64`,
      `aarch64`), macOS (`x86_64`, `aarch64`), and Windows MSVC (`x86_64`).
    - `toolchain-rust.cmake` / `corrosion/`: Rust/Cargo target integration with
      CMake via Corrosion.
    - `android.cmake`: Core helper macros (`android_add_executable`,
      `android_add_library`, `android_add_test`, `android_install_shared`,
      symbol extraction, license metadata).
    - `prebuilts.cmake`: Resolves prebuilt library targets from
      `$AOSP/prebuilts/android-emulator-build/`.
    - `emu-windows-libs.cmake`: Locates Windows SDK, ATL/MFC, DIA SDK, and
      Windows ADK (`DismApi`) libraries on Windows.

- **`toolchains.json`**:
  - Pins the Clang compiler version
    (`prebuilts/clang/host/<os>-x86/clang-<version>`) and Rust version
    (`prebuilts/rust/<os>-x86/<version>`) used by the build.
